Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:56:48

Release 0.1.0. Initial release

Changelog: 10-10-2026 18:12:32

New app ace-queues: opens the BC-250's dedicated compute (ACE) queues for games. bc250-ace-queues.sh builds a
patched RADV for the system's Mesa version in a Fedora container (the Mesa source checked against the Mesa release
maintainers' signature; one patch, mesa/gfx1013-ace-queue.patch, from DryhoppedIPA/bc250-gfx1013-fix as trimmed
for Bazzite by tri3gubki-ops/bc250-async-compute-bazzite), installs it in /usr/local/lib/bc250-ace-queues beside
the system Mesa, and runs its own ACE queue test (acetest/: fills, copies, an image round trip and a partial
dispatch on every queue at once, ten device lifetimes, plus a kernel-log check for ring timeouts). Games use the
driver through the launch options wrapper bc250-ace-queues-run, which only selects it when the test passed with
the running kernel and the installed driver. "All apps" (environment.d and profile.d) can only be switched on after
a passed test; a boot check (bc250-ace-queues-guard.service) switches it off when the kernel or the driver
changed. The window shows the four steps (build, install, test, use) and runs the root steps through pkexec. The
installer puts the app root-owned in /opt with its bc250_core and uses the suite's shared venv. The logo is a
placeholder.
